Appendix H: IEC 60287 Ampacity Calculation Details

H.1 General ampacity equation. The ampacity of a buried cable is given by IEC 60287-1-1:

I = \sqrt{\frac{\Delta\theta - W_d \cdot [T_1/2 + n(T_2 + T_3 + T_4)]}{R \cdot [T_1 + n(1 + \lambda_1)T_2 + n(1 + \lambda_1 + \lambda_2)(T_3 + T_4)]}},

where:

· \Delta\theta = conductor temperature rise above ambient
· W_d = dielectric loss per unit length
· T_1 = thermal resistance of insulation
· T_2 = thermal resistance of bedding
· T_3 = thermal resistance of outer covering
· T_4 = thermal resistance of surrounding soil
· R = AC resistance per unit length
· n = number of loaded conductors
· \lambda_1, \lambda_2 = sheath and armour loss factors

H.2 Soil thermal resistance. For a cable buried at depth L_b in soil of thermal resistivity \rho_{\rm soil}:

T_4 = \frac{\rho_{\rm soil}}{2\pi} \ln\left( \frac{2L_b}{D_e} \right),

where D_e is the external diameter of the cable.

H.3 Derating factors. The derating factor for soil thermal resistivity is:

f_{\rm soil} = \sqrt{\frac{\rho_{\rm soil, ref}}{\rho_{\rm soil}}},

where \rho_{\rm soil, ref} = 1.0 K·m/W is the reference value.

For \rho_{\rm soil} = 2.5 K·m/W:

f_{\rm soil} = \sqrt{\frac{1.0}{2.5}} = 0.632.

For \rho_{\rm soil} = 1.5 K·m/W:

f_{\rm soil} = \sqrt{\frac{1.0}{1.5}} = 0.816.

The reference value f_{\rm soil} = 0.70 corresponds to \rho_{\rm soil} \approx 2.04 K·m/W.

H.4 Grouping factor. For two loaded conductors (positive and negative) in the same trench, the grouping factor is f_{\rm group} \approx 0.85.

H.5 Total derating. The effective current density is:

J_{\rm eff} = J_{\rm air} \cdot f_{\rm soil} \cdot f_{\rm group} \cdot f_{\rm harm}.

For J_{\rm air} = 3 A/mm², f_{\rm soil} = 0.70, f_{\rm group} = 0.85, f_{\rm harm} = 0.98:

J_{\rm eff} = 3 \cdot 0.70 \cdot 0.85 \cdot 0.98 = 1.75\ \text{A/mm}^2.

The conservative value J_{\rm eff} = 1.5 A/mm² includes an additional safety margin.

