Appendix J: Discriminating Kernel Computation Details

J.1 State space. The state vector is:

x = (q_{\rm elec}, V_{\rm DC}, SOC_{\rm bat}) \in \{0,1,2\} \times \mathbb{R}^+ \times [0,1].

J.2 Dynamics.

Electrical mode q_{\rm elec}:

\dot{q}_{\rm elec} = f_q(q_{\rm elec}, d_{\rm elec}),

where d_{\rm elec} is the disturbance (source loss, converter failure).

DC bus voltage:

\dot{V}_{\rm DC} = \frac{P_{\rm gen}(q_{\rm elec}) - P_{\rm load}}{C_{\rm bus} V_{\rm DC}}.

Battery state of charge:

\dot{SOC} = -\frac{P_{\rm crit}}{E_{\rm bat}} \quad \text{if } q_{\rm elec} = 2,

\dot{SOC} = 0 \quad \text{if } q_{\rm elec} \in \{0,1\}.

J.3 Safe set.

\mathcal{C}_{\rm safe} = \{(q, V, SOC) : V \ge V_{\min},\ SOC \ge SOC_{\min}\}.

J.4 Operational envelope.

\mathcal{K} = \{(q, V, SOC) : q \in \{0,1,2\},\ V_{\min} \le V \le V_{\max},\ SOC_{\min} \le SOC \le SOC_{\max}\}.

J.5 Disturbance set.

\mathcal{D} = \{d_1, d_2, d_3\},

where:

· d_1: loss of one AC source (q: 0 \to 1)
· d_2: loss of both AC sources (q: 1 \to 2)
· d_3: converter failure (q: \text{any} \to 2)

J.6 Discriminating kernel. The discriminating kernel is:

\operatorname{Disc}_{\rm elec} = \{x_0 : \exists u(\cdot), \forall d(\cdot), \exists T \ge 0, x(T) \in \mathcal{C}_{\rm safe}, x(t) \in \mathcal{K}\ \forall t \in [0,T]\}.

J.7 Under-approximation via ellipsoids. Using the ellipsoid method, the discriminating kernel is under-approximated by:

\operatorname{Disc}_{\rm elec}^{\rm under} = \left\{ (q, V, SOC) : V \ge V_{\min} + \Delta V_{\rm decay}(T_{\rm ride}),\ SOC \ge SOC_{\min} + \frac{P_{\rm crit}^{\rm cont} \cdot T_{\rm ride}}{E_{\rm bat}} \right\}.

J.8 Numerical evaluation. For V_{\min} = 2700 V, V_0 = 3000 V, C_{\rm bus} = 12 mF, \Delta P = 100 kW, T_{\rm ride} = 100 ms:

\Delta V_{\rm decay}(T_{\rm ride}) = V_0 - \sqrt{V_0^2 - \frac{2 \Delta P \cdot T_{\rm ride}}{C_{\rm bus}}}.

= 3000 - \sqrt{9 \times 10^6 - \frac{2 \cdot 100\,000 \cdot 0.1}{0.012}} = 3000 - \sqrt{9 \times 10^6 - 1.667 \times 10^6}.

= 3000 - \sqrt{7.333 \times 10^6} = 3000 - 2708 = 292\ \text{V}.

For SOC_{\min} = 0.2, P_{\rm crit}^{\rm cont} = 1.5 kW, T_{\rm ride} = 30 s, E_{\rm bat} = 1 kWh:

\Delta SOC = \frac{1500 \cdot 30}{3.6 \times 10^6} = \frac{45\,000}{3\,600\,000} = 0.0125.

The under-approximated kernel is:

\operatorname{Disc}_{\rm elec}^{\rm under} = \{(q, V, SOC) : V \ge 2700 + 292 = 2992\ \text{V},\ SOC \ge 0.2 + 0.0125 = 0.2125\}.

J.9 Conclusion. The discriminating kernel is non-empty. The admissibility condition:

\mathcal{K}_{\rm operating} \subseteq \operatorname{Disc}_{\rm elec}^{\rm under}

is satisfied if the initial state satisfies V \ge 2992 V and SOC \ge 0.2125.

